examples within their stated situation rather than turning them into universal rules. Resolve local references and enumeration ranges to exactly their antecedent; a rule for a listed subset must not extend to later items in the same topic. Keep claims about a named example or demonstration attached to that example, rather than the entire category. Preserve the anchor of relative time expressions including an event's start or end, without shifting when an example occurs. When reproducing an expression or demonstration, preserve its symbols and ordering instead of paraphrasing it into a different expression. Retain necessary qualifiers in the same field and assertion that states the claim; a qualified key point cannot justify an unqualified assertion in the overview. Choose the length each topic needs to preserve its essential meaning. Long, information-dense sources may need a fuller overview and more developed points. Do not force a fixed character count or omit essential conditions to shorten the text. Stay concise by removing repetition; do not pad the output to fill the available budget. Return strict JSON only with keys \"summary\" (string) and \"key_points\" (array of 1-14 strings). Example JSON shape (replace placeholders with source facts): {\"key_points\":[\"...\"],\"summary\":\"...\"}"
